{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"TreeAlgorithms"}],"externalID":"s:14TreeAlgorithms21LowestCommonAncestorsV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LowestCommonAncestors","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"LowestCommonAncestors","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LowestCommonAncestors","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestor.swift#L76","fileName":"LowestCommonAncestor.swift"},"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct"},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LowestCommonAncestors","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For vertices at preorder positions p < q, the answer is the vertex at the least position among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parents of the vertices at positions p + 1 … q: those parents lie in the answer’s subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and include it, and it has the least position there. So a query is one range minimum over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 parent positions (the Euler tour reduction on half the entries), answered by 64-entry"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"blocks with a bitmask of each prefix’s minimum stack and a sparse table over the blocks’ minima."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"About two words per vertex, plus (n\/64)·log₂(n\/64) for the table."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/lowestcommonancestors"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Lowest common ancestors of a rooted tree or arborescence, each in O(1) after O(n) work","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"lowest_common_ancestor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", JGraphT’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"LowestCommonAncestorAlgorithm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/init(_:)-6re9c","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/init(_:)-9p0ha"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/distance(from:to:)","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/distance(fromIndex:toIndex:)","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/lowestCommonAncestor(of:_:)","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/lowestCommonAncestor(ofIndex:_:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgor